Course.start({"num":10,"unit":2,"slug":"m10-familia-posesivos","minutes":45,"title":"La familia, hay y los posesivos","subtitle":"Family words, there is / there are, and my, your, his, our","lede":"Spanish has no *'s*. To say whose something is, you use possessive words like *mi* and *nuestro*, or the little word *de*.","recap":"Last time you made adjectives agree with their nouns (**las flores amarillas**) and learned where they go in a sentence.","context":{"title":"Las Meninas","place":"Museo del Prado, Madrid","text":"In **1656**, the painter **Diego Velázquez** finished one of the most famous paintings in the world, **Las Meninas** (*The Ladies-in-Waiting*). In the middle stands the little princess, the **Infanta Margarita**, five years old, surrounded by her maids, a dog, and members of the royal household.\n\nLook closely, and you'll find Velázquez himself on the left, standing at a huge canvas with his brush. And in a small mirror on the back wall are two blurry faces: the princess's **father and mother**, King Philip IV and Queen Mariana. Are they standing where *you* are, looking in? People have argued about this painting for over 350 years.\n\nIt's a family portrait with a twist. In Spanish you could say: {{En el cuadro hay muchas personas. La niña es la hija del rey. Sus padres están en el espejo.}}"},"learn":[{"title":"La familia","text":"Tap each card. A masculine plural can mean a mixed group: **los padres** = *parents*, **los hermanos** = *brothers and sisters*.","flash":[["el padre · la madre","father · mother"],["los padres","parents"],["el hermano · la hermana","brother · sister"],["los hermanos","siblings"],["el abuelo · la abuela","grandfather · grandmother"],["el tío · la tía","uncle · aunt"],["el primo · la prima","cousin"],["el hijo · la hija","son · daughter"],["el esposo · la esposa","husband · wife"],["el sobrino · la sobrina","nephew · niece"],["el padrastro · la madrastra","stepfather · stepmother"],["la mascota","pet"]]},{"title":"Possessive adjectives: whose is it?","text":"Possessive adjectives go **before** the noun and match **the thing owned**, not the owner. *Mi* becomes **mis** for more than one thing; *nuestro* and *vuestro* also change for gender.","table":{"head":["Owner","One thing","More than one"],"rows":[["my","{{mi hermano}}","{{mis hermanos}}"],["your (tú)","{{tu prima}}","{{tus primas}}"],["his, her, its, your (usted)","{{su perro}}","{{sus perros}}"],["our","{{nuestro tío}} · {{nuestra tía}}","{{nuestros tíos}} · {{nuestras tías}}"],["your (vosotros)","{{vuestro abuelo}} · {{vuestra abuela}}","{{vuestros abuelos}} · {{vuestras abuelas}}"],["their, your (ustedes)","{{su casa}}","{{sus casas}}"]]},"tip":"*Nuestra casa* (our house): *nuestra* is feminine because **casa** is feminine, even if the owners are boys. And **tu** (your) has no accent; **tú** (you) does."},{"title":"*De* for possession, and *hay*","text":"Spanish has no *'s*. Instead, say *the dog **of** Ana*: {{el perro de Ana}}. If *su* is unclear, *de* helps: {{la casa de ella}} (*her house*).\n\n**Hay** means *there is* or *there are*, for one thing or many: {{Hay un gato.}} {{Hay cinco personas en mi familia.}} To ask *how many*: {{¿Cuántas personas hay en tu familia?}} To say *there isn't*: {{No hay perros en la foto.}}","tip":"*De* + *el* combines into **del**: {{la hija del rey}} (*the king's daughter*). *De la* doesn't change."}],"tasks":[{"id":"t1","type":"match","title":"La familia","intro":"Tap a Spanish word (you'll hear it), then its meaning.","pairs":[["la abuela","grandmother"],["el tío","uncle"],["la prima","cousin (female)"],["los padres","parents"],["el hermano","brother"],["la hija","daughter"],["la esposa","wife"],["el sobrino","nephew"],["la mascota","pet"]],"hints":["*Padres* looks like *fathers*, but it usually means *parents*."]},{"id":"t2","type":"select","title":"Choose the possessive","intro":"Choose the word that matches the noun.","items":[{"s":"{mis|mi} hermanos ((my))"},{"s":"{Nuestra|Nuestro|Nuestras} casa es pequeña. ((our))"},{"s":"{tus|tu} primas ((your))"},{"s":"Ana y {sus|su} padres ((her))"},{"s":"{nuestros|nuestro|nuestras} abuelos ((our))"},{"s":"Señor López, ¿es {su|tu} hijo? ((your, formal))"},{"s":"{mi|mis} familia ((my))","why":"*Familia* is one group, so **mi**."},{"s":"{vuestras|vuestros|vuestra} tías ((your, vosotros))"}],"hints":["Look at the noun after the blank, not at the owner.","Formal *your* (usted) is **su**."]},{"id":"t3","type":"cloze","title":"Write the possessive","intro":"Write the Spanish word for the English one in parentheses.","items":["[nuestros] ((our)) abuelos","[mis] ((my)) tías","[tu] ((your, tú)) perro","[sus] ((their)) padres","[nuestra] ((our)) familia","[su] ((his)) hermana","[su] ((your, usted)) hijo","[vuestra] ((your, vosotros)) casa"],"hints":["**su / sus** can mean *his, her, its, their* or formal *your*.","*Nuestro* changes for gender: *nuestra familia*, *nuestros abuelos*."]},{"id":"t4","type":"read","title":"La familia de Elena","intro":"Read (and listen to) Elena's description of her family, then answer the questions.","passage":"{{Me llamo Elena. En mi familia hay cinco personas: mi padre, mi madre, mis dos hermanos y yo.}} {{Mi padre se llama Jorge y es de Cuba. Mi madre se llama Ana.}} {{Mis hermanos se llaman Luis y Tomás.}} {{En casa también hay una mascota: nuestro perro, Coco.}}\n\n{{Los padres de mi madre son mis abuelos, Pedro y Carmen.}} {{Mi tía Rosa es la hermana de mi padre. Sus hijos, Marta y Sergio, son mis primos.}}","questions":[{"q":"How many people are in Elena's family?","choices":[["five",true],["four",false],["six",false],["three",false]]},{"q":"Who is from Cuba?","choices":[["her father",true],["her mother",false],["her grandparents",false],["her aunt",false]]},{"q":"Who is Coco?","choices":[["the family dog",true],["Elena's cousin",false],["Elena's sister",false],["the family cat",false]]},{"q":"Pedro and Carmen are…","choices":[["her mother's parents",true],["her father's parents",false],["her aunt and uncle",false],["her cousins",false]]},{"q":"Whose children are Marta and Sergio?","choices":[["Aunt Rosa's",true],["Jorge's",false],["Pedro's",false],["Ana's",false]]}],"hints":["*Los padres de mi madre* = *my mother's parents*.","*Sus hijos* here = *her children* (Rosa's)."]},{"id":"t5","type":"translate","title":"Whose is it?","intro":"Translate. Remember: no *'s* in Spanish.","items":[{"en":"Ana's dog","es":["el perro de ana"]},{"en":"my brother's friends","es":["los amigos de mi hermano"]},{"en":"There are four people in my family.","es":["hay cuatro personas en mi familia","en mi familia hay cuatro personas"]},{"en":"There isn't a cat.","es":["no hay [un] gato"]},{"en":"Our cousins are from Texas.","es":["nuestros primos son de texas","nuestras primas son de texas"]}],"hints":["*X's Y* → **el Y de X**.","*There is / there are* → **hay**. *There isn't* → **no hay**."]},{"id":"t6","type":"errors","title":"Fix the mistakes","intro":"Tap the wrong word, then type the correct one.","items":[{"s":"Mis hermana es alta.","bad":"Mis","fix":"Mi"},{"s":"Nuestro familia es grande.","bad":"Nuestro","fix":"Nuestra"},{"s":"Su padres son de Cuba.","bad":"Su","fix":"Sus"},{"s":"Mis primos son nuestro amigos.","bad":"nuestro","fix":"nuestros"},{"s":"¿Cuántos personas hay en tu familia?","bad":"Cuántos","fix":"Cuántas","why":"*Personas* is feminine."}],"hints":["Each possessive must match the noun right after it."]},{"id":"s1","type":"speak","title":"Talk about your family","intro":"Listen, record, compare.","items":[{"s":"En mi familia hay cuatro personas."},{"s":"Mi abuela es la madre de mi padre."},{"s":"Nuestro perro se llama Max."}]}],"build":{"heading":"Mi familia","prompt":"Describe your family, or a family from a book, show or movie. Write **at least 6 sentences**. Say how many people there are with **hay**, use at least **three different possessives** (*mi, mis, su, nuestro…*), at least **four family words**, and at least one **de** for possession.","model":"{{En mi familia hay cinco personas.}} {{Mis padres se llaman Carlos y Julia.}} {{Mi hermana es simpática y mi hermano es muy gracioso.}} {{Nuestra casa es pequeña pero bonita.}} {{La hermana de mi madre es mi tía Laura.}} {{Sus hijos son mis primos favoritos.}}","placeholder":"En mi familia hay…","reqs":[{"t":"At least 6 sentences","sentences":6},{"t":"**hay** to count people or things","any":["hay"]},{"t":"Three different possessives","any":["mi","mis","tu","tus","su","sus","nuestro","nuestra","nuestros","nuestras","vuestro","vuestra","vuestros","vuestras"],"min":3},{"t":"Four family words","any":["padre","padres","madre","papá","mamá","hermano","hermana","hermanos","hermanas","abuelo","abuela","abuelos","abuelas","tío","tía","tíos","tías","primo","prima","primos","primas","hijo","hija","hijos","hijas","esposo","esposa","sobrino","sobrina","padrastro","madrastra","mascota","familia"],"min":4},{"t":"Possession with **de** (*la casa de…*)","re":"\\b(el|la|los|las)\\s+\\p{L}+\\s+(de|del)\\s+\\p{L}+"}]},"reflect":{"q":"Velázquez painted himself right into the royal family's portrait. Who would you paint into *your* family portrait? Think about people who are like family to you even if you aren't related: a coach, a neighbor, a friend. Why do they belong in the picture?","placeholder":"In my family portrait, I would include…"},"further":{"id":"x1","type":"quiz","title":"Challenge: *su* can mean many things","questions":[{"q":"*Marta y su hermano.* Whose brother?","choices":[["Marta's (her brother)",true],["my brother",false],["our brother",false],["your (tú) brother",false]]},{"q":"How can you make *su casa* clearly mean *their house*?","choices":[["la casa de ellos",true],["la casa su",false],["su casa de",false],["sus casa",false]]},{"q":"*La hija ___ rey* (the king's daughter)","choices":[["del",true,"*de + el = del*"],["de el",false],["de la",false],["al",false]]}]},"culture":"**¿Sabías?** In Spanish-speaking countries, people often have **two last names**: the father's first last name, then the mother's. If Juan García López and María Ruiz Pérez have a daughter named Ana, she is **Ana García Ruiz**.","unitTitle":"¿Cómo eres? Sustantivos y descripciones","code":"NjU2MS1TQU5JTkVN","prev":"m09-adjetivos.html","next":"m11-verbos-ar.html"});
